          body: "Types of loss: actual, perceived, anticipatory, situational; grief, bereavement, mourning; Kübler-Ross stages not a timetable; Worden's tasks; dual process. Complicated grief: prolonged, delayed, exaggerated, masked; risk after sudden, violent, stigmatised deaths and the death of a child; refer for suicidal thoughts and inability to function. Disenfranchised grief — stillbirth, miscarriage. Children: under 5 death is reversible, 5–9 final but may feel to blame, 10+ adult understanding; say 'died', never 'asleep' or 'gone away'. Support: sit, stay, say the name, listen, allow anger; never 'God's will', 'better place', 'be strong', 'you can have another'. Palliative care: active total care, early, neither hastens nor postpones, team, family in the unit of care; morphine oral regular with breakthrough, laxative; breathlessness — fan, position, low-dose morphine; nausea by cause; mouth care; fungating wound — metronidazole gel; advance care planning and DNACPR documented and handed over. Dying: more sleep, no food, no drink, no swallow — stop oral drugs; cool mottled limbs; Cheyne–Stokes; death rattle — side, hyoscine, explain, no suction; terminal restlessness — pain, bladder, bowel, hypoxia first; stop observations, bloods and IV fluids; anticipatory subcutaneous medicines — morphine, midazolam, hyoscine, haloperidol; mouth care hourly; turn 2–4 hourly; family present, hearing persists, faith leader in time; cultural practices asked and accommodated; home if wished. Death: time noted; confirm — no pulse, heart sounds or breathing for one minute, pupils fixed and dilated, no response; doctor certifies; next of kin in person; coroner cases — unexpected, violent, within 24 h of admission, peri-operative, custody — do not wash, leave all tubes. Family: time alone, wishes asked, property listed by two and signed for. Last offices: two nurses, standard precautions, flat with one pillow, eyes closed, jaw supported, dentures in, tubes per policy, wounds dressed, wash, two identification bands wrist and ankle plus shroud label, body bag for VHF and cholera, dignified transfer, documentation. Debrief the staff.",
